<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n65265" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάχαιρ-α</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μᾰ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ας</span></span> (later -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ης</span>, dat. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῃ</span>, <i><span class="en">
			<u>PTeb.</u>
			16.14
		</span></i>
		<span class="entity">(ii B. C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
			<u>Ev.Luc.</u>
			21.24
		</span></i>, etc.), ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>large knife</i> or <i>dirk</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				11.844
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				18.597
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				19.252
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. ἥ οἱ πὰρ ξίφεος μέγα κουλεὸν
					αἰὲν ἄωρτο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					3.271
				</span></i>
			; <i>carving-knife</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				1.49
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.61
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				489
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				353a
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοπίδες μ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Cyc.</u>
					242
				</span></i>
			; <i>sacrificial knife</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pax</u>
				948
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.Com.
				91
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Michel</u>
				832.52
			</span></i> (Samos, <span class="entity">iv B. C.</span>):—<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ Δελφικὴ μ.</span> a knife adapted to
			various purposes, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1252b2
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δελφικὴ μ.</span>
			; prov., of greedy persons, because Delphian sacrificers
			claimed a share for the knife, <i><span class="en">
				<u>App.Prov.</u>
				1.94
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> as a weapon,
				<i>short sword, dagger</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				4.59
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				6.75
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				7.225
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				13.87
			</span></i>, etc.; an assassin's weapon, <i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				5.69
			</span></i>; used by jugglers, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Euthd.</u>
				294e
			</span></i> (pl.), etc.; later, <i>sabre</i>, opp. the straight sword
				(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξίφος</span>), <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				12.11
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>HG</u>
				3.3.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				1.2.13
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Matt.</u>
				26.52
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἐπὶ τῆς μ.</span>, of
			a bodyguard, <i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>Epict.</u>
				1.30.7
			</span></i>; but, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ μ. τασσόμενοι</span>
			possessing power of life and death (<i>jus gladii), Cat.Cod.
				Astr.</i><i><span class="en">
				8(4).173
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. ἱππική</span> cavalry
				<i>sabre,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				11(2).161
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>B</u>
				99
			</span></i> (Delos, <span class="entity">iii B. C.</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. κουρίδες</span>, <i>shears</i> or
				<i>scissors</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Cratin.
				37
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεκαρμένος μοιχὸν μιᾶ
			μ.</span>, i.e. with one <i>blade</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				849
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				2.32
			</span></i> (where <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διπλῇ</span> is f.l.), <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μιᾷ μαχαίρᾳ; μ.
				κουρικαί</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Dio</u>
				9
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διὰ μαχαιρῶν καὶ πυρός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Zen.
					3.19
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Posidipp.
				1.10
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. τοῦ πνεύματος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ep.Eph.</u>
					6.17
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Is.</u>
				49.2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> name of a
			precious stone, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mir.</u>
				847a5
			</span></i>, Ps.-<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Fluv.</u>
				10.5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> part of the
			liver, <i><span class="en">
				Ruf.
				<u>Onom.</u>
				180
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
